*  RPOEM_driver - drives RPOEM.SNO, which generates poems from a sample
*  grammar.  Contract per RPOEM.sno header.  RPOEM carries its own END, so a
*  driver can only be the include; it opens its own input file and needs no
*  stdin.  See the batch-E FINDING for why no oracle .ref accompanies this
*  driver: RPOEM needs BOTH the four-argument INPUT(.INPUT,5,,'rpoem.in')
*  association, which Spitbol refuses with ERROR 116, AND RANDOM.sno, whose
*  real-argument REMDR CSNOBOL4 refuses with Error 1, Illegal data type.
*  Neither sanctioned oracle can run it, so it is UNSCOREABLE rather than
*  red -- and supplying the lowercase rpoem.in the module asks for was
*  tried and does not change that, because the RANDOM wall is behind it.
-INCLUDE "RPOEM.sno"
